@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_DataTable}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Usage}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Styling}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Data_Table @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Content_Styling</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Data_Table @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Content_Styling</h1>
<p>
    There are numerous ways to apply styling and they can be used individually or combined. You can if you wish use both CellStyleFunc and CellStyle on the same cell.
</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        RowStyleFunc: a function that accepts a row of data and returns a string containing css property value pairs which get placed inside a <span class="code-span">style</span> attribute added to the row (tr element).
    </li>
    <li>
        CellStyleFunc:  a function that accepts a row of data and returns a string containing css property value pairs which get placed inside a <span class="code-span">style</span> attribute added to the cell (td element).
    </li>
    <li>
        HeaderStyle: a string containing css property value pairs which get placed inside a <span class="code-span">style</span> attribute added to the column header (th element).
    </li>
    <li>
        CellStyle: a string containing css property value pairs which get placed inside a <span class="code-span">style</span> attribute added to the cell header (td element).
    </li>
    <li>
        CellFormat: although not strictly styling I have included it here for convenience. This takes and applies standard .NET format strings to formattable data types.
    </li>
</ul>
<p>
   For this example I have used all of the above with 10K rows. To see the RowStyleFunc filter using the text "Ki" as it applies a row style to contacts available in the United Kingdom. 
   See below for information on everything that has been applied as it may not be obvious on first glance.
</p>

<DataTable TData="Contact" DataSource="@_dataSource" Title="Contact Results" PagerBinding="@_pagerBinding" FilterRule="_filterRule" RowStyleFunc=UKAvailability>
    <Filter>
        <DebounceFilter HintText="Filters across first name, surname and country" RegexPattern="^[A-Za-z ]*$" OnDebounceFilterResult="HandleOnDebounce"
                        ValidationMessage="Invalid filter, filtering paused, letters and spaces only" />
    </Filter>
    <TableColumns>
        <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.ContactID"   DisplayName="ID"            IsSortable="true" />
        <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.GivenName"   DisplayName="First Name"    IsSortable="true" />
        <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.FamilyName"  DisplayName="Surname"       IsSortable="true" />
        <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.Country"     DisplayName="Country"       IsSortable="true" CellStyle="white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis;" HeaderStyle="min-width:16ch;" /> 
            
            
        <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.DateOfBirth" DisplayName="Date of Birth" ColumnAlignment="ColumnAlignment.Centre" IsSortable="true" CellFormat="yyyy-MM-dd" HeaderStyle="min-width:16ch;" />
        <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.Rate"        DisplayName="Hourly Rate"   IsSortable="true" CellFormat="C" ColumnAlignment="ColumnAlignment.End" />
        <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.Availability" IsSortable="true" ColumnAlignment="ColumnAlignment.Centre" 
            CellStyleFunc='r => r.Availability == "Unavailable" ? "font-weight:bold; color:red;" : String.Empty' />
    </TableColumns>
    <BottomPager>
        <Pager @bind-CurrentPage="@_pagerBinding.CurrentPage" AriaLabel="Contacts pager" TotalItemCount="@_pagerBinding.TotalItemCount" CurrentItemCount="@_pagerBinding.CurrentItemCount"
               ItemsPerPage="@_pagerBinding.ItemsPerPage" PagerSelectorType="PagerSelectorType.Button" ShowFirstLast="true" PageAlignment="PageAlignment.End" AddApplicationRole="true" />
    </BottomPager>
</DataTable>
<p>
    By default the table defines the widths for the columns as it sees fit breaking content values if necessary. You can control this behaviour by specifying min-widths or widths on the columns concerned.
</p>

<p>
    For the country column I added a min-width of 16ch using the <span class="code-span">HeaderStyle</span> parameter, but the more interesting thing, and you may need to
    minimize the width of the browser window to see it, is I also used the Countries <span class="code-span">CellStyle</span> parameter to set a text-overflow:ellipsis. As a side note
    this is only a visual thing, screen reader users get the full text. Its a useful technique for saving space.
</p>
<p>
    As well as the aforementioned RowStyleFunc, I also applied a CellStyleFunc on the Availability column that just makes the text bold and red when the value is Unavailable.
</p>
<p>
    For the Date of Birth column, I did two things, I added a HeaderStyle to stop the dates characters breaking and gave the CellFormat the .NET string format value of "yyyy-MM-dd" (ISO 8601 date format).
</p>
<p>
    You will have most likely realised from all of the examples I have also been using a CellFormat value of "C" (currency) to display (your) locale currency symbol.
</p>

<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Left_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_DataTable}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Usage}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Selecting}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Data_Table - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Selecting</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Right_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_DataTable}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Usage}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Templating}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Data_Table - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Templating</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
</div>

@code {

    private Func<Contact, bool>? _filterRule = null;
    private PagerBinding _pagerBinding = new(currentPage: 0, currentItemCount: 0, totalItemCount: 0, itemsPerPage: 10);
    private List<Contact> _dataSource = [];

    private Func<Contact, string?>? UKAvailability = c => c.Availability == "Available" && c.Country == "United Kingdom" ? "background-color:var(--br-unit-colour-success); color:white;" : null;

    protected override void OnInitialized()

        => _dataSource = StaticData.GetContacts(10_000);

    private async Task HandleOnDebounce(DebouncedFilterResult debounceResult)
    {
        if (debounceResult.IsValid)
        {
            _filterRule = (data) => data.GivenName.Contains(debounceResult.FilterValue, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                                    || data.FamilyName.Contains(debounceResult.FilterValue, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                                    || data.Country.ToString().Contains(debounceResult.FilterValue, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

            /*
                * The debounce uses a Func not an EventCallback to negate renders if the filter value is invalid so
                * you call StateHasChanged if all is well.
            */
            await InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
        }
    }
}